    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Check NWS updates here Thunderstorms with heavy rain will cause minor flooding in the following counties... Faribault...Freeborn...Le Sueur...Steele...Blue Earth...Waseca... Rice... * Until 330 AM CDT Thursday. * At 925 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This will cause urban and small stream flooding in the area. Within this region, there are several pockets that have seen 2 to 4 inches of rain this evening. This heavy rain will likely result in ponding of water in low areas. * Some locations that will experience minor flooding include... Mankato, Owatonna, Faribault, Northfield, Albert Lea, North Mankato, Waseca, Blue Earth, Lake Crystal, Eagle Lake, Wells, and Janesville.",
